; EditFade -- WaveSmith's Effects menu in FS-UAE under MuForce and
; MuGuardianAngel (DEV:mutools), on PAL hires 640x256: a copy of the test
; single, Fade.wav (its level map beside it as Fade.prl), worked by
; DEV:Test/EditFade.rexx at the places the trace (DEV:Test/fade.trace)
; gives: a part faded in by Right-Amiga F, another faded out from the
; menu, Undo and Redo, Save, Quit. After the run, on the host:
;   python3 tools/make_edit_single.py --check dist/Test/Edit Fade --trace dist/Test/fade.trace
; replays the save at its levels: every sample of the faded parts as
; WaveSmith's sums make it, the rest byte for byte, the map's looks moved
; by their level.
;
;   gmake autotest T=EditFade W=pal LIMIT=300
FailAt 21
Wait 8
Execute DEV:mutools
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/fade.trace DEV:Test/Edit/Fade.wav DEV:Test/Edit/Fade.prl DEV:Test/Edit/Fade.wav.info ENV:WaveSmith.prefs QUIET
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/edit-fade-#? QUIET
Echo >DEV:Test/auto.log "EditFade"
Version >>DEV:Test/auto.log DEV:sasc/WaveSmith FULL
Copy >NIL: DEV:Test/Edit/Single.wav DEV:Test/Edit/Fade.wav
Copy >NIL: DEV:Test/Edit/Single.prl DEV:Test/Edit/Fade.prl
SetEnv WaveSmithTrace DEV:Test/fade.trace
Run >NIL: DEV:sasc/WaveSmith DEV:Test/Edit/Fade.wav
Wait 10
RX DEV:Test/EditFade.rexx
Wait 3
Echo >>DEV:Test/auto.log "still running:"
Status >>DEV:Test/auto.log COMMAND=DEV:sasc/WaveSmith
UnSetEnv WaveSmithTrace
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
